WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.725
So who names the device now?

2
00:00:01.725 --> 00:00:05.013
The short answer: whatever
provisions it, at build time.

3
00:00:05.013 --> 00:00:10.088
For Windows, that's usually Autopilot,
which sets up a new PC out of the box.

4
00:00:10.088 --> 00:00:13.148
Classic Autopilot with
Microsoft Entra join,

5
00:00:13.148 --> 00:00:17.979
which joins the PC to Microsoft's cloud
directory instead of AD, has a name

6
00:00:17.979 --> 00:00:20.556
template: fifteen characters or fewer,

7
00:00:20.556 --> 00:00:23.938
with macros for the serial
number or random digits.

8
00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:27.338
Hybrid join, which
joins both AD and Entra,

9
00:00:27.338 --> 00:00:30.638
gets only a prefix,
and the rest is random.

10
00:00:30.638 --> 00:00:35.082
The newer Autopilot device preparation
now has a name template too,

11
00:00:35.082 --> 00:00:36.987
up to sixty-three characters.

12
00:00:36.987 --> 00:00:41.257
The caveat matters: it works only
for devices with device association,

13
00:00:41.257 --> 00:00:45.675
and has no effect on devices onboarded
with corporate identifiers only.

14
00:00:45.675 --> 00:00:49.711
As an inference, the Federal
Modernization Workbook's Book 05's

15
00:00:49.711 --> 00:00:53.825
description of device preparation
needs a review against this.

16
00:00:53.825 --> 00:00:58.658
After enrollment, Intune's Rename action
can rename corporate-owned Windows

17
00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:02.962
PCs and Macs, but not hybrid-joined
devices, which need domain methods.

18
00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:06.354
Macs have no enrollment-time
name template that I found;

19
00:01:06.354 --> 00:01:08.124
you rename after enrollment.

20
00:01:08.124 --> 00:01:11.587
Linux takes its name from
cloud-init or a static hostname.

21
00:01:11.587 --> 00:01:15.563
Azure Arc keeps the server's
hostname as a fixed resource name.

22
00:01:15.563 --> 00:01:18.112
Cloud VMs get names at create time.

23
00:01:18.112 --> 00:01:25.693
Sources: Microsoft Learn: Autopilot device
preparation Entra join policy [S1],

24
00:01:25.693 --> 00:01:33.393
Compare device preparation and Autopilot
[S2], Entra join Autopilot profile [S3],

25
00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:39.553
Hybrid join Domain Join profile
[S4], Rename a device in Intune [S5],

26
00:01:39.553 --> 00:01:44.884
Accounts CSP [S6], macOS
automated device enrollment [S7];

27
00:01:44.884 --> 00:01:51.044
hostnamectl and hostname(5) [S10,
S11]; cloud-init Set Hostname [S12];

28
00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:57.441
azcmagent connect and Arc rename
[S15, S16]; Azure ComputerName [S17];

29
